          "claim": "For $k^2=z$ the regular radial solution is $\\varphi_l(k,r)=r^{l+1}\\sum_{n\\ge0}c_nr^n$, with $c_0=1$ and $c_n=-(\\gamma c_{n-1}+k^2c_{n-2})/[n(n+2l+1)]$, $c_{-1}=0$. On compact $k$ sets choose $C\\ge\\max(1,\\gamma,|k|)$; induction gives $|c_n|\\le C^n/n!$, since $[\\gamma/C+|k|^2(n-1)/C^2]/(n+2l+1)\\le1$. The series and its compact derivatives converge, giving a solution entire in $k$, real for real $k$, with regular coefficient one. Compact-interval continuation is given by the ordinary Volterra IVP series: for the first-order system its $n$th iterated integral is bounded by $M^nL^n/n!$ uniformly on compact parameter sets, proving uniqueness, continuity, and holomorphic dependence rather than using a real-parameter theorem as a holomorphic premise.",
